From aee101e4550b8fd273671649092a3ff24984a6bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add Samsung S5K3P9/3J1/3M3/4HA/2L4 sensor drivers
 and AK7374

Raw Bayer sensors of the Galaxy S10 family cameras:

 - s5k3p9: 16 MP, ultra-wide camera; analogue gain control in sensor
   codes (1/32 steps).
 - s5k3j1: 10 MP, front camera.
 - s5k3m3: 12 MP, telephoto camera, with a frame descriptor.
 - s5k4ha: 8 MP, second front camera of the Galaxy S10+, with a frame
   descriptor.
 - s5k2l4: 12 MP, main rear wide camera, including the full-resolution
   4032x3024 mode at 2054 Mbit/s; the native Bayer order is GBRG.

The drivers provide native size and crop selection targets and claim
the shared MCLK pin only while a sensor is powered. S5K3M3 and S5K2L4
write their controls under a grouped parameter hold; S5K3M3, S5K4HA and
S5K2L4 log the sensor's frame counter after stream-on and its state
before stream-off.

ak7375: add the AK7374 voice coil driver of the camera lenses (9 bit
position like the AK7345, standby mode like the AK7375); the product
ID is logged at the first power-on, and the supplies are switched off
again when the first write after power-on fails.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
